        "authors": [
            {
                "id": null,
                "preferredName": "P. Kimber",
                "firstName": "P.",
                "lastName": "Kimber"
            }
        ],
        "abstract": "For truly autonomous systems the exchange, distribution and use of collectively available information implies that individual system elements have both a commonly understood exchange language and a commonly understood context for meaning. This presentation addressed requirements issues and needs for the development of a unified information exchange mechanism for autonomous systems, including formal exchange standards, information metadata, information uncertainties, and context properties, all of which lead to implications for processing, understanding and distributing information.",
